From: lean <chenlin@fnnas.com>
Subject: [PATCH] nss-ecm: use kernel_bind for the route netlink socket

The bind callback now takes sockaddr_unsized in newer stable kernels.
Use the kernel socket wrapper and a type-neutral address pointer so the
netlink address works with both old and new signatures.

Signed-off-by: lean <chenlin@fnnas.com>
---
--- a/ecm_interface.c
+++ b/ecm_interface.c
@@ -8209,7 +8209,7 @@
 	saddr.nl_groups = RTNLGRP_LINK;
 	saddr.nl_pid    = current->pid;
 
-	err = __ewn.sock->ops->bind(__ewn.sock, (struct sockaddr *)&saddr, sizeof(struct sockaddr));
+	err = kernel_bind(__ewn.sock, (void *)&saddr, sizeof(saddr));
 	if (err < 0) {
 		DEBUG_ERROR("failed to bind sock\n");
 		goto exit2;
